    },
    {
      "source_id": "oj-reg-2026-1744",
      "pinpoint": "Art. 1, point (40)(a): Art. 113, third paragraph, point (a), application from 2 December 2026"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "oj-reg-2026-1744",
      "pinpoint": "Recitals 11 to 13"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "oj-dir-2011-93",
      "pinpoint": "Art. 2, points (c) and (e); Art. 5(1) ('without right')"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "oj-reg-2024-1689",
      "pinpoint": "Art. 3, points (3), (4), (6), (7), (9) and (11)"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "consolidated-ai-act-2026-07-27",
      "pinpoint": "Art. 5(1)(bb), (1a); Art. 113 (cross-check only)"
    }
  ],
  "interpretations": [
    {
      "id": "C2-use-limb",
      "text": "Art. 5(1a)(b) is read literally: the use is prohibited only where the deployer uses the system for the purpose of generating or manipulating such material or performance; the content element stays and the Art. 5(1a)(a) conditions do not apply to use."
    },
    {
      "id": "C3-roles",
      "text": "Providers (Art. 3(3)) and importers (Art. 3(6)) place on the market or put into service and are tested under Art. 5(1a)(a); deployers (Art. 3(4)) use and are tested under Art. 5(1a)(b). A distributor makes available (Art. 3(7)), which is not the first making available that Art. 3(9) calls placing on the market, so a distributor-only profile stays UNKNOWN and goes to review."
    },
    {
      "id": "C10-without-right",
      "text": "Whether a 'without right' defence applies under national law (Art. 5(1)(bb) AIA; Directive 2011/93/EU, Art. 5(1); Recital 13 of Regulation (EU) 2026/1744) is a fact the reviewer establishes; the engine does not evaluate national law."
    }
  ],
